6. Vibe sharing

Sharing makes Vibes discoverable through Arvdoul's existing social graph.

6.1 Sharing options

Support:

- Share to a direct conversation.
- Share to a group conversation.
- Share to eligible connections.
- Copy a permitted Vibe link.
- Use the existing system share mechanism where appropriate.

Sharing must respect the Vibe's visibility rules.

6.2 Share preview

The preview should include:

- Creator identity.
- Vibe thumbnail where permitted.
- Content type.
- Appropriate expiration information.
- Link to the Vibe where access is authorized.

Do not expose private media through public preview metadata.

6.3 Sharing rules

- Private Vibes cannot be publicly forwarded.
- Selected-audience Vibes cannot be shared with unauthorized recipients.
- Expired Vibes cannot be opened through old shares.
- Deleted Vibes cannot be opened through old shares.
- Blocked users cannot use sharing to bypass restrictions.
- Group members must be evaluated individually where necessary.

A share record does not grant access to the underlying Vibe.

6.4 Sharing data

Logical model:

interface VibeShare {
  id: string;

  vibeId: string;
  senderId: string;

  destinationType:
    | "direct"
    | "group"
    | "link"
    | "system";

  destinationId?: string;

  createdAt: Timestamp;
}

Use existing message attachment models when possible.

6.5 External links

If external Vibe links are supported:

- Use unguessable identifiers.
- Do not expose private media URLs.
- Require authentication where appropriate.
- Recheck current authorization on access.
- Enforce expiration.
- Enforce deletion.
- Avoid permanent access tokens.
- Apply abuse protection.


