9. Social graph integration

Vibes must understand Arvdoul's actual relationship model.

9.1 Relationship types

Integrate with existing:

- Followers.
- Connections.
- Friend relationships.
- Friend requests.
- Close Circle.
- Blocks.
- Mutes.
- Restrictions.

Do not invent a new relationship system.

9.2 Permission matrix

Evaluate the relationship between creator and viewer for every sensitive operation.

Relationship	View	Reply	Share

Eligible public viewer	Subject to visibility	Subject to reply policy	Subject to sharing policy
Follower	Subject to visibility	Subject to reply policy	Subject to sharing policy
Connection	Subject to visibility	Subject to reply policy	Subject to sharing policy
Close Circle member	Subject to visibility	Subject to reply policy	Subject to sharing policy
Selected viewer	Only if selected	Subject to reply policy	Subject to sharing policy
Blocked user	No	No	No
Restricted user	According to restriction policy	Restricted	Restricted
Creator	Own Vibes	Not applicable	Subject to sharing policy


This table describes general behavior, not automatic permissions. The authoritative audience configuration and social graph must determine the final decision.

9.3 Relationship changes

Handle:

- Follow/unfollow.
- Connection request accepted.
- Connection removed.
- Close Circle membership added.
- Close Circle membership removed.
- Block.
- Unblock.
- Restriction.
- Account suspension.
- Account deletion.

Permission changes must take effect without requiring users to reinstall the application.


