12. XP and levels integration

XP represents progression and participation, not currency.

Coins and XP must remain separate systems.

12.1 XP objectives

Vibes should contribute to meaningful platform activity.

Possible qualifying actions:

- Publishing an eligible Vibe.
- Completing a meaningful Vibe interaction.
- Receiving genuine engagement.
- Maintaining legitimate creative activity.
- Reaching verified participation milestones.

Not every action should automatically generate XP.

12.2 XP policy

Do not reward:

- Repeatedly opening the same Vibe.
- Repeated self-interactions.
- Spam publishing.
- Artificial reaction loops.
- Automated engagement.
- Repeatedly creating and deleting content.
- Duplicate event submissions.
- Manipulated engagement.
- Fake accounts.

XP must be awarded according to a centralized progression policy.

12.3 Suggested XP event architecture

interface VibeXPEvent {
  id: string;

  userId: string;

  vibeId?: string;

  eventType:
    | "vibe_published"
    | "vibe_engagement_milestone"
    | "vibe_creator_milestone"
    | "vibe_activity_milestone";

  xpAmount: number;

  sourceEventId: string;

  createdAt: Timestamp;

  status:
    | "pending"
    | "approved"
    | "rejected";
}

The actual XP amount must come from the existing progression engine.

The event model must support idempotency and fraud controls.

12.4 Publishing XP

A legitimate publishing action may qualify for progression.

However:

- Apply rate limits.
- Exclude spam.
- Avoid rewarding repeated uploads of identical content.
- Enforce meaningful participation conditions.
- Prevent duplicate XP from retries.
- Avoid creating an incentive to flood the Vibes Feed.

12.5 Engagement XP

If engagement contributes to creator XP, it must be based on qualified, authentic events.

Do not award unlimited XP for every view.

Use appropriate thresholds, eligibility rules and time windows.

12.6 Level progression

When users earn enough XP:

- Update progression through the existing level engine.
- Calculate the new level server-side.
- Record the progression event.
- Trigger the appropriate notification.
- Update the user's profile identity.
- Preserve historical progression.

Do not calculate authoritative levels independently in multiple frontend components.


