21. Performance and scalability

Part 2 adds more interactions and cross-system dependencies. The implementation must avoid making Vibes slower or more expensive.

21.1 Frontend performance

- Lazy-load interaction panels.
- Avoid unnecessary Viewer rerenders.
- Debounce appropriate search inputs.
- Use optimistic updates only where safe.
- Reconcile optimistic state with authoritative responses.
- Avoid repeated profile lookups.
- Avoid unnecessary listeners.
- Paginate reaction and reply details.
- Cache appropriate non-sensitive metadata.

21.2 Firestore efficiency

- Use bounded queries.
- Avoid unbounded reaction reads.
- Avoid unnecessary writes.
- Batch appropriate updates.
- Use aggregate counters carefully.
- Avoid updating a highly contended document on every event.
- Use sharding or alternative aggregation for high-volume counters when justified.
- Design indexes around actual queries.
- Monitor read/write costs.

21.3 Messaging performance

- Avoid duplicating Vibe media.
- Store references rather than copies.
- Paginate conversations.
- Avoid repeated conversation lookups.
- Handle unavailable attachments efficiently.

21.4 Notification performance

- Deduplicate events.
- Batch where appropriate.
- Avoid notification storms.
- Respect user preferences before delivery.
- Separate in-app persistence from push delivery.
- Retry failed external delivery safely.

21.5 Economy performance

- Use authoritative transaction processing.
- Avoid unnecessary wallet reads.
- Avoid duplicate ledger entries.
- Keep transaction operations minimal.
- Monitor transaction failures and contention.


